  "body": "Currently the spec uses the final fetched response URL to set the worker's global scope url in step 13.3 here:\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#worker-processing-model\r\n\r\nThis means that worker `self.location`, base URL, etc should contain the final URL if the script was redirected.  Also, if a service worker passes a response with a URL to `respondWith()` then the spec would also expose that URL here.\r\n\r\nI wrote a glitch to test the simple redirect case:\r\n\r\nhttps://redirect-worker-test.glitch.me/\r\n\r\nCurrently only firefox implements this step.  All the other browsers show the original URL.\r\n\r\nSince there is only one browser implementing this step, should it be kept?  I personally feel like we should keep the step setting the final URL, but I was curious if there was an argument to remove it.",
